  "@type": "Recipe",
  "recipeCuisine": "Japan",
  "name": "Tonkatsu Curry",
  "text": "Tonkatsu Curry\n\nPreparation time:\n\nCooking time:\n\nYield: 2 servings\n\nIngredients\n\nFor the curry\n\n1 large onion (chopped),\n\n1/2 onion (chopped in 2x2cm pieces)\n\n100g carrot (coarsely grated),\n\n2 aubergine (peeled in strips, and then chunked with a rolling cut),\n\n2 small bell peppers (cut into 2x2cm pieces),\n\n2 cloves of garlic (finely grated),\n\nginger (finely grated),\n\n1 tbsp curry powder,\n\n2 tbsp olive oil,\n\n200cc canned tomato,\n\n300cc Water (1.27 u.s. cup)\n\n1 Soup Stock Cube\n\n1 Dried Bay Leaf\n\n25g Medium Spicy Curry Block (0.88oz)\n\n1/2 Small apple (peeled, soaked in salt water)\n\nRelishes\n\nFukujinzuke\n\nRakkyo\n\nFor the tonkatsu\n\n2 slices of 1.2cm thick Pork Loin ( 1/2 inch thick)\n\nFlour\n\nBeaten Egg (1/2 Egg & 1/2 tsp Water)\n\nPanko - Bread Crumbs\n\nFrying Oil\n\nA pinch of Salt\n\nA pinch of Pepper\n\nPreparation\n\n1. Add oil to a saute pan and fry the chopped onions until golden brown (5 minutes).\n\n2. Add the coarsely grated carrot and fry for 2-3 minutes.\n\n3. Add the grated garlic and ginger until fragrant.\n\n4. Turn the heat low and add the curry powder, frying for 2 minutes.\n\n5. Add the aubergine and onions.\n\n6. Add the chopped tomatoes.\n\n7. Add water and crumble in the stock cube.\n\n8. Add the dry bay leaf.\n\n9. Put the lid on a simmer for 10 minutes.\n\n10. Turn off the heat and add the chopped curry block. Stir until combined.\n\n11. Grate the apple into the mixture.\n\n12. Add the bell pepper.\n\n13. Turn the heat back on and simmer with the lid on until the pepper is soft (2 minutes).\n\n14. Season the pork.\n\n15. Make cuts along the stringy parts of the port.\n\n16. Lightly coat with flour, then egg wash, then breadcrumbs.\n\n17. Shallow fry until golden brown.",
  "recipeYield": "2 servings",
